WEBVTT

00:02.342 --> 00:04.469
KATARA: Water.

00:04.719 --> 00:06.387
Earth.

00:06.721 --> 00:08.598
Fire.

00:08.890 --> 00:10.642
Air.

00:11.267 --> 00:14.646
Long ago, the four nations lived
together in harmony.

00:15.313 --> 00:19.234
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.359 --> 00:23.780
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

00:23.905 --> 00:26.741
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.158 --> 00:30.828
100 years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

00:30.954 --> 00:32.705
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.830 --> 00:35.124
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:35.208 --> 00:37.794
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.877 --> 00:38.920
AANG: Oof!

00:39.170 --> 00:41.881
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:10.872 --> 01:14.042
Spare coins for weary travelers?

01:14.167 --> 01:15.377
( COINS CLINKING )

01:15.919 --> 01:17.963
This is humiliating. We're royalty.

01:18.088 --> 01:20.548
These people should be
giving us whatever we want.

01:20.674 --> 01:23.134
They will, if you ask nicely.

01:25.303 --> 01:29.599
Spare change for a hungry old man?

01:30.016 --> 01:31.977
Aw, here you go.

01:32.477 --> 01:38.358
The coin is appreciated,
but not as much as your smile.

01:38.650 --> 01:39.985
( GIGGLES )

01:41.861 --> 01:44.864
How about some entertainment
in exchange for...

01:45.031 --> 01:46.616
A gold piece?

01:46.825 --> 01:48.785
We're not performers.

01:49.286 --> 01:51.162
Not professional, anyway.

01:51.830 --> 01:56.710
♪ It's a long, long way to Ba Sing Se

01:56.793 --> 02:02.507
♪ But the girls in the city
They look so pretty ♪

02:02.924 --> 02:05.593
Come on, we're talking a gold piece here.

02:05.677 --> 02:06.761
Let's see some action.

02:08.096 --> 02:09.597
Dance.

02:09.723 --> 02:14.102
♪ They kiss so sweet
That you really have to meet

02:14.477 --> 02:18.606
♪ The girls from Ba Sing Se ♪

02:18.982 --> 02:22.027
( LAUGHING )

02:22.152 --> 02:25.155
Nothing like a fat man
dancing for his dinner.

02:25.280 --> 02:26.614
Here you go.

02:29.534 --> 02:32.579
Such a kind man.

02:39.002 --> 02:40.503
( CHATTERS )

02:55.602 --> 02:58.855
Hey, you taking us down for a reason?

02:59.272 --> 03:01.608
Aang, why are we going down?

03:01.733 --> 03:02.859
What?

03:02.984 --> 03:04.194
I didn't even notice.

03:04.736 --> 03:06.863
SOKKA: Are you noticing now?

03:07.113 --> 03:08.281
Is something wrong?

03:08.531 --> 03:10.283
I know this is gonna sound weird,

03:10.408 --> 03:13.328
but I think the swamp is... calling to me.

03:13.411 --> 03:15.872
Is it telling you where we
can get something to eat?

03:15.955 --> 03:19.542
AANG: No, I, I think it wants us
to land there.

03:19.667 --> 03:20.835
No offense to the swamp,

03:20.919 --> 03:23.505
but I don't see any land there to land on.

03:23.588 --> 03:24.589
I don't know.

03:24.672 --> 03:27.801
Bumi said to learn earthbending,
I would have to wait and listen.

03:27.926 --> 03:30.095
And now, I'm actually hearing the earth.

03:30.220 --> 03:31.721
Do you want me to ignore it?

03:31.846 --> 03:32.889
( CHATTERS )

03:33.014 --> 03:34.641
- Yes.
- I don't know.

03:35.100 --> 03:37.811
There's something ominous
about that place.

03:38.436 --> 03:39.938
( CHATTERS )

03:40.188 --> 03:41.314
( GRUMBLES )

03:41.398 --> 03:43.900
See? Even Appa and Momo
don't like it here.

03:44.109 --> 03:48.488
Okay, since everyone feels so
strongly about this, bye, swamp.

03:48.780 --> 03:50.198
Yip yip!

03:51.991 --> 03:54.994
( RUMBLING )

03:55.495 --> 03:58.206
SOKKA: You better throw in an extra yip.
We gotta move.

04:08.675 --> 04:09.759
Ahh!

04:10.760 --> 04:11.886
( YELLING )

04:25.859 --> 04:28.695
ALL: ( SCREAMING )

04:35.535 --> 04:36.703
( GROANS )

04:39.539 --> 04:41.040
Where's Appa and Momo?

04:47.505 --> 04:48.923
Appa!

04:49.048 --> 04:50.508
Momo!

04:54.137 --> 04:56.014
Sokka, you've got an elbow leech.

04:56.139 --> 04:57.432
Where, where?

04:57.557 --> 04:59.851
Where do you think?

04:59.976 --> 05:02.729
Why do things keep attaching to me?

05:04.439 --> 05:06.191
You couldn't find them?

05:06.316 --> 05:07.358
No...

05:07.484 --> 05:10.528
And the tornado, it just disappeared.

05:16.326 --> 05:18.411
-( GRUMBLING )
-( CHATTERS )

05:21.289 --> 05:22.540
( ROARS )

05:44.395 --> 05:46.814
( ROARS )

05:47.982 --> 05:49.234
We better speed things up.

05:51.069 --> 05:53.863
Maybe we should be a little
nicer to the swamp.

05:54.197 --> 05:55.615
Aang, these are just plants.

05:55.740 --> 05:57.742
Do you want me to say please and thank you

05:57.825 --> 05:59.744
as I swing my machete back and forth?

05:59.869 --> 06:01.496
Maybe you should listen to Aang.

06:01.913 --> 06:05.458
Something about this place feels... alive.

06:05.625 --> 06:08.419
I'm sure there are lots of things
that are alive here.

06:08.670 --> 06:11.256
And if we don't want to wind
up getting eaten by them,

06:11.381 --> 06:13.841
we need to find Appa as fast as we can.

06:37.282 --> 06:38.575
( BLOWS WHISTLE )

06:38.700 --> 06:39.742
( ROARS )

06:41.369 --> 06:42.495
( BLOWS WHISTLE )

06:42.620 --> 06:44.664
( GURGLES )

06:47.166 --> 06:48.293
KATARA: Appa!

06:48.543 --> 06:50.128
Momo?

06:50.378 --> 06:53.172
There's no way they can hear us
and no way we can see them.

06:53.548 --> 06:55.550
We'll have to make camp for the night.

06:56.301 --> 06:58.720
-( INSECTS BUZZING )
- Ah, ugh!

06:59.679 --> 07:00.847
What was that?

07:01.472 --> 07:03.057
Nothing, just swamp gas.

07:03.141 --> 07:05.560
Look, there's nothing
supernatural going on here.

07:06.019 --> 07:07.103
ALL: Ugh...

07:07.228 --> 07:08.938
( HUMAN-LIKE SCREAMS )

07:09.063 --> 07:10.565
( SCREAMS )

07:11.065 --> 07:13.192
I think we should build a fire.

07:16.613 --> 07:18.072
Sokka, the longer we're here,

07:18.156 --> 07:20.325
the more I think you
shouldn't be doing that.

07:20.617 --> 07:21.743
No, I asked the swamp.

07:21.826 --> 07:24.370
It said this was fine. Right, swamp?

07:24.621 --> 07:26.664
( SQUEAKILY ) No problem, Sokka.

07:32.545 --> 07:35.632
Does anyone else get the feeling
that we're being watched?

07:35.923 --> 07:38.885
Please, we're all alone out here.

07:39.385 --> 07:41.054
( GRUNTING )

07:44.849 --> 07:47.352
Except for them.

07:47.560 --> 07:49.520
Right, except for them.

07:50.438 --> 07:53.232
( FROGS CROAKING )

07:53.691 --> 07:59.030
( INDISTINCT ANIMAL NOISES )

08:03.368 --> 08:06.579
( ROARS )

08:07.288 --> 08:09.749
( ANIMAL NOISES STOP )

08:36.275 --> 08:37.485
ALL: ( YELLING )

08:37.610 --> 08:38.611
Hagh!

08:38.736 --> 08:39.737
Ahh!

08:39.821 --> 08:41.072
Ahh!

08:55.128 --> 08:56.963
( GRUNTING )

09:07.014 --> 09:08.641
Ugh.

09:12.437 --> 09:13.479
Ahh!

09:13.730 --> 09:14.856
Ugh...

09:20.737 --> 09:22.739
Guys?

09:27.618 --> 09:30.204
What'd you reckon
make a track like that, Tho?

09:30.413 --> 09:31.789
Don't know, Due.

09:31.873 --> 09:35.918
Something with six legs,
pretty big 'uns, too.

09:36.544 --> 09:38.504
DUE: Leaves a nice, wide trail to follow.

09:38.963 --> 09:41.007
You know what's at the end of that trail?

09:42.633 --> 09:44.093
Dinner.

09:55.188 --> 09:57.231
( ROARS )

10:03.029 --> 10:04.071
( GROWLS )

10:04.489 --> 10:05.698
( HISSING )

10:08.659 --> 10:10.244
( GRUMBLES )

10:16.793 --> 10:18.085
KATARA: Aang?

10:18.544 --> 10:20.254
Sokka?

10:23.049 --> 10:24.091
Hello?

10:24.175 --> 10:25.843
Hello.

10:25.927 --> 10:27.470
Can you help me?

10:29.096 --> 10:30.807
Mom?

10:30.890 --> 10:32.308
Mom!

10:35.686 --> 10:37.480
I can't believe...

10:37.897 --> 10:40.024
( GASPS )

10:40.900 --> 10:42.944
( SOBBING )

10:47.824 --> 10:49.450
Aang!

10:49.909 --> 10:53.204
Stupid swamp. Dumb, ugly vines.

10:53.704 --> 10:55.331
Katara!

10:55.790 --> 10:57.917
You think you're so tough, huh?

10:58.000 --> 10:59.335
( GRUNTING )

10:59.418 --> 11:00.628
Ah!

11:04.924 --> 11:07.218
Hello?

11:10.721 --> 11:12.181
Yue?

11:12.431 --> 11:14.600
This is just a trick of the light...

11:14.809 --> 11:16.018
Swamp gas.

11:16.102 --> 11:18.229
I hit my head running away last night.

11:18.437 --> 11:20.481
I'm going crazy.

11:22.817 --> 11:25.444
( ECHOING ) You didn't protect me.
You didn't protect me.

11:27.947 --> 11:29.282
( SIGHS )

11:29.365 --> 11:30.700
Ah!

11:38.457 --> 11:41.294
Katara!

11:41.836 --> 11:43.212
Appa!

11:44.505 --> 11:45.548
Hello?

11:45.673 --> 11:47.300
Who are you?

11:47.425 --> 11:48.801
( LAUGHING )

11:48.926 --> 11:50.011
AANG: Hey!

11:50.136 --> 11:51.387
Come back.

11:53.514 --> 11:54.765
( LAUGHING )

11:58.936 --> 12:00.605
( GIGGLES )

12:07.236 --> 12:09.322
( LAUGHS )

12:25.922 --> 12:27.590
Lookee there, Tho.

12:27.673 --> 12:30.176
Is that a little hairy
fella riding that thing?

12:30.384 --> 12:32.595
No, that's what they call a "Iemu."

12:32.887 --> 12:36.349
Saw one at a traveling show once.
Real smart, they say.

12:36.432 --> 12:38.559
Bet he tastes a lot like possum-chicken.

12:38.643 --> 12:41.270
You think everything tastes
like possum-chicken.

12:41.479 --> 12:44.732
Come on, now, fellas,
just a little closer.

12:44.815 --> 12:46.400
Nice and easy.

12:46.609 --> 12:47.944
Nothin' to worry about.

12:48.027 --> 12:49.487
We just fixin' to eat ya.

12:50.029 --> 12:51.364
( GROWLS )

12:51.489 --> 12:52.865
What'd ya say that fer?

12:52.949 --> 12:54.116
Well, we are.

12:54.200 --> 12:55.993
But you don't have to tell them that.

12:56.077 --> 12:57.870
How'd I know they'd understand me?

12:57.954 --> 12:59.997
Come on.

13:19.392 --> 13:21.352
( LAUGHING )

13:26.941 --> 13:28.901
Who are you?

13:33.155 --> 13:34.824
BOTH: Ahh!

13:35.574 --> 13:36.659
Ugh.

13:36.742 --> 13:37.827
ALL: ( GROANING )

13:38.703 --> 13:40.579
What do you guys think you're doing?

13:40.663 --> 13:42.873
I've been looking all over for you.

13:42.957 --> 13:45.251
Well, I've been wandering
around looking for you.

13:45.459 --> 13:47.378
I was chasing some girl.

13:47.586 --> 13:49.463
- What girl?
- I don't know.

13:50.006 --> 13:52.717
I heard laughing, and I saw
some girl in a fancy dress.

13:52.967 --> 13:54.760
Well, there must be a tea party here,

13:54.844 --> 13:57.138
and we just didn't get our invitations.

13:57.972 --> 13:59.807
I thought I saw Mom.

14:02.143 --> 14:04.103
Look, we were all just scared and hungry,

14:04.186 --> 14:06.105
and our minds were playing tricks on us.

14:06.188 --> 14:08.024
That's why we all saw things out here.

14:08.149 --> 14:09.859
You saw something, too?

14:09.942 --> 14:11.110
I thought I saw Yue.

14:11.360 --> 14:12.903
But that doesn't prove anything.

14:13.279 --> 14:15.281
Look, I think about her all the time.

14:15.531 --> 14:17.616
And you saw Mom, someone you miss a lot.

14:17.950 --> 14:19.493
What about me?

14:19.577 --> 14:21.162
I didn't know the girl I saw.

14:21.454 --> 14:23.831
And all our visions led us right here.

14:24.165 --> 14:27.376
Okay, so where's here,
the middle of the swamp?

14:27.460 --> 14:28.919
Yeah...

14:29.003 --> 14:31.297
The center.

14:32.965 --> 14:34.425
It's the heart of the swamp.

14:34.508 --> 14:35.843
It's been calling us here.

14:36.093 --> 14:37.386
I knew it.

14:37.678 --> 14:40.806
It's just a tree. It can't call anyone.

14:41.057 --> 14:43.350
For the last time,
there's nothing after us,

14:43.434 --> 14:46.437
and there's nothing
magical happening here.

14:46.520 --> 14:49.565
ALL: ( SCREAMING )

15:12.088 --> 15:14.256
Ahh!

15:14.882 --> 15:16.008
( GRUNTING )

15:26.143 --> 15:27.311
( GRUNTS )

15:38.239 --> 15:40.491
Ah!

15:41.117 --> 15:42.535
Ugh!

15:49.500 --> 15:50.584
KATARA: ( GROANS )

15:51.335 --> 15:53.337
- Ahh!
- Unh!

16:02.972 --> 16:04.098
( GROWLING )

16:12.398 --> 16:14.191
Ah!

16:15.985 --> 16:18.070
( GRUNTING )

16:18.904 --> 16:21.907
Now, what would a "Iemu" need a shirt fer?

16:22.032 --> 16:23.075
Ahh!

16:23.200 --> 16:25.202
Ugh!

16:35.296 --> 16:37.298
( GROWLING )

16:44.263 --> 16:45.931
( GRUNTING )

17:03.991 --> 17:05.951
BOTH: Ugh!

17:12.625 --> 17:13.626
Ah!

17:15.961 --> 17:17.004
Ugh.

17:17.713 --> 17:19.798
( SCREAMING )

17:19.882 --> 17:20.966
Ugh!

17:35.439 --> 17:38.359
There's someone in there!
He's bending the vines.

17:39.360 --> 17:40.778
( GRUNTS )

17:46.033 --> 17:47.117
Ah!

17:52.414 --> 17:55.000
Why did you call me here
if you just wanted to kill us?

17:55.542 --> 17:57.127
Wait!

17:57.211 --> 17:59.255
I didn't call you here.

18:01.215 --> 18:03.926
We were flying over, and I heard
something calling to me,

18:04.009 --> 18:05.010
telling me to land.

18:05.177 --> 18:06.512
He's the Avatar.

18:06.595 --> 18:08.472
Stuff like that happens to us a lot.

18:08.555 --> 18:10.182
The Avatar?

18:10.266 --> 18:11.517
Come with me.

18:14.436 --> 18:16.313
KATARA: So who are you, then?

18:16.939 --> 18:19.942
I protect the swamp from
folks that want to hurt it,

18:20.025 --> 18:22.027
like this fellow with his big knife.

18:22.152 --> 18:23.362
See?

18:23.487 --> 18:25.364
Completely reasonable. Not a monster,

18:25.447 --> 18:27.283
just a regular guy defending his home.

18:27.408 --> 18:29.618
Nothing mystical about it.

18:30.577 --> 18:33.580
MAN: Oh, the swamp is a mystical place,
all right.

18:33.706 --> 18:34.832
It's sacred.

18:35.457 --> 18:39.586
I reached enlightenment right here,
under the banyan grove tree.

18:39.670 --> 18:42.756
I heard it calling me, just like you did.

18:43.632 --> 18:46.593
Sure you did. It seems real chatty.

18:47.970 --> 18:51.265
See, this whole swamp
is actually just one tree

18:51.390 --> 18:53.225
spread out over miles.

18:53.309 --> 18:56.353
Branches spread and sink and take root

18:56.437 --> 18:58.856
and then spread some more...

18:58.939 --> 19:01.567
One big, living organism,

19:01.650 --> 19:04.820
just like the entire world.

19:06.030 --> 19:10.200
I get how the tree is one big thing,
but the whole world?

19:10.284 --> 19:11.285
Sure.

19:11.493 --> 19:13.162
You think you're any different

19:13.245 --> 19:16.081
from me or your friends or this tree?

19:16.498 --> 19:18.334
If you listen hard enough,

19:18.417 --> 19:21.837
you can hear every living thing
breathing together.

19:21.920 --> 19:24.923
You can feel everything growing.

19:25.549 --> 19:29.345
We are all living together,
even if most folks don't act like it.

19:29.803 --> 19:32.014
We all have the same roots,

19:32.139 --> 19:35.601
and we are all branches of the same tree.

19:35.851 --> 19:37.728
KATARA: But what did our visions mean?

19:37.811 --> 19:41.440
In the swamp, we see visions
of people we've lost,

19:41.648 --> 19:45.361
people we loved, folks we think are gone.

19:45.486 --> 19:50.324
But the swamp tells us they're not.
We're still connected to 'em.

19:50.449 --> 19:54.244
Time is an illusion, and so is death.

19:54.536 --> 19:56.330
But what about my vision?

19:56.413 --> 19:57.915
It was someone I had never met.

19:58.332 --> 20:00.542
You're the Avatar. You tell me.

20:01.418 --> 20:04.046
Time is an illusion...

20:04.838 --> 20:08.133
So, it's someone I will meet.

20:09.760 --> 20:13.263
Sorry to interrupt the lesson,
but we still need to find Appa and Momo.

20:13.555 --> 20:15.599
I think I know how to find them.

20:15.974 --> 20:18.435
Everything is connected.

20:37.121 --> 20:38.914
Come on, we've gotta hurry!

20:39.415 --> 20:42.626
♪ Set my lines by the riverbed

20:42.960 --> 20:46.213
♪ Caught ten fish, and I killed 'em dead

20:46.338 --> 20:49.174
♪ Cut 'em and gut 'em
And I toss the heads

20:49.258 --> 20:52.886
♪ In the water
To keep them cat-gators fed ♪

20:55.180 --> 20:57.182
( SCREAMING )

20:58.434 --> 20:59.768
Appa!

21:00.644 --> 21:02.020
Oh!

21:02.104 --> 21:03.814
We're under attack!

21:07.734 --> 21:09.987
Hey, you guys are waterbenders.

21:10.571 --> 21:11.697
You, too?

21:11.780 --> 21:13.740
That means we're kin.

21:19.121 --> 21:21.081
Hey, Huu. How you been?

21:21.457 --> 21:26.462
You know, scared some folks,
swung some vines... The usual.

21:26.920 --> 21:28.172
Huu?

21:28.255 --> 21:31.758
( TWANGY MUSIC PLAYING )

21:31.967 --> 21:33.760
How you like that possum-chicken?

21:33.844 --> 21:35.804
Tastes just like arctic hen.

21:36.054 --> 21:38.474
So why were you guys
so interested in eating Appa?

21:38.557 --> 21:41.143
You've got plenty of those
big things wandering around.

21:41.351 --> 21:43.187
You want me to eat ol' Slim?

21:43.437 --> 21:46.064
He's like a member of the family.

21:46.482 --> 21:47.816
Nice Slim.

21:47.941 --> 21:49.693
-( GROWLS )
- Ah!

21:50.068 --> 21:52.696
( LAUGHING ) Oh, he don't eat no bugs.

21:52.779 --> 21:54.198
That's people food.

21:54.531 --> 21:56.200
Where'd you say you was from?

21:56.283 --> 21:57.451
The South Pole.

21:57.618 --> 22:00.120
Didn't know there was
waterbenders anywhere but here.

22:00.204 --> 22:02.206
They got a nice swamp there, do they?

22:02.289 --> 22:04.791
No, it's all ice and snow.

22:05.292 --> 22:07.669
Hmm, no wonder you left.

22:07.794 --> 22:09.296
Well, I hope you realize now

22:09.379 --> 22:11.924
that nothing strange was going on here.

22:12.007 --> 22:14.301
Just a bunch of greasy people
living in a swamp.

22:14.468 --> 22:16.136
What about the visions?

22:16.261 --> 22:18.388
I told you, we were hungry.

22:18.472 --> 22:20.933
I'm eating a giant bug.

22:22.100 --> 22:23.977
Mmm-ugh.

22:24.061 --> 22:27.105
But what about when the tree showed me
where Appa and Momo were?

22:27.314 --> 22:29.274
That's Avatar stuff, that doesn't count.

22:29.399 --> 22:31.026
The only thing I can't figure out

22:31.109 --> 22:33.362
is how you made the tornado
that sucked us down.

22:33.570 --> 22:35.822
I can't do anything like that.

22:35.906 --> 22:38.450
I just bend the water in the plants.

22:39.326 --> 22:41.161
Well, no accounting for weather.

22:41.453 --> 22:44.831
Still, there's absolutely
nothing mysterious about the swamp.

22:49.044 --> 22:50.212
( SCREAMS )

22:50.337 --> 22:51.380
( THWACKS )

22:59.721 --> 23:01.473
Who's there?

23:04.643 --> 23:05.852
